  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The outer zone – 3v3 with jokers along the boards",
  "description": "Split the rink into a playing zone in the middle and two narrow outer zones along the boards, about 2 metres wide. Play 3v3 in the playing zone. 1–2 jokers (J) in the outer zones play for whichever team has the puck, for example one on each half.\n\nThe attacking team must pass to a joker before they may shoot. Goals can also be scored straight from an outer zone. Young players tend to crowd around the puck – this game teaches them to use the width and link up play.\n\nPlay for example 2 × 5 minutes and change jokers. Keep pucks by the nets so the goalie can restart quickly when the puck goes dead. Play lengthwise or across the rink depending on age.\n\nProgression: jokers in the outer zone may take the puck off each other, or remove the jokers and give extra points for goals that come via an outer zone.\n\nNot to scale. The goalies are not drawn.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Spread out – make the middle bigger by not crowding the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Jokers: skate along the boards so the puck carrier can always find you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Pass out to the outer zone when the opponents have bunched up in the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Goalie: try to reach a player in the outer zone straight away when restarting."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 2,
